1
00:00:07,161 --> 00:00:11,252
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:12,489 --> 00:00:13,635
Yuhh...

3
00:00:13,635 --> 00:00:17,578
It smells like butt-rock in
here. I'm leaving.

4
00:00:17,578 --> 00:00:21,665
Oh, wait, I can't go back.
They're bombing.

5
00:00:21,665 --> 00:00:25,422
I know what, I'll go and ask that security
guard if he knows how to get out of here.

6
00:00:25,422 --> 00:00:29,274
Come to think of it, I'm not sure
why I didn't do that in the first place.

7
00:00:29,274 --> 00:00:32,008
Ehh, I guess we were both
kind of distracted.

8
00:00:32,008 --> 00:00:32,765
What?

9
00:00:32,765 --> 00:00:35,384
Did that collapse under its own weight?

10
00:00:35,384 --> 00:00:38,301
I've made stronger pillow forts than that!

11
00:00:38,301 --> 00:00:41,373
Though, to be fair, my
pillow forts were pretty bad ass.

12
00:00:41,373 --> 00:00:45,219
I used to soak them in plaster of Paris
and would let them dry to reinforce them.

13
00:00:45,219 --> 00:00:47,101
That sure pissed mom off.

14
00:00:47,101 --> 00:00:49,716
But, in the end, I think it was worth it.

15
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:51,196
Where is everybody?

16
00:00:51,196 --> 00:00:52,522
Not up there...

17
00:00:52,522 --> 00:00:54,051
the guard's gone...

18
00:00:54,051 --> 00:00:56,758
I think I remember some
explosives here...?

19
00:00:56,758 --> 00:00:59,179
Now there's just scorch marks...

20
00:00:59,179 --> 00:01:00,817
A blood stain...

21
00:01:00,817 --> 00:01:04,912
And this is after... firing...
that rocket...

22
00:01:04,912 --> 00:01:06,163
Huh...

23
00:01:06,163 --> 00:01:08,250
Well, I'll take these grenades anyway.

24
00:01:08,250 --> 00:01:12,065
I'm not so upper-class I won't
accept grenades in worn condition.

25
00:01:12,065 --> 00:01:14,178
They're just going to explode anyway.

26
00:01:14,178 --> 00:01:15,937
So, where am I going now?

27
00:01:15,937 --> 00:01:17,060
Uhh...

28
00:01:17,060 --> 00:01:19,038
Oh, hey, that blew a hole down there.

29
00:01:19,038 --> 00:01:20,817
May as well check that out.

30
00:01:20,817 --> 00:01:24,698
I'm still not happy with the trend
of going down, but, y'know,

31
00:01:24,698 --> 00:01:26,616
anywhere's better than here.

32
00:01:26,616 --> 00:01:27,875
I think.

33
00:01:27,875 --> 00:01:30,238
So, hey, that means that was the whole alien.

34
00:01:30,238 --> 00:01:33,292
I was afraid I was going to
look down there and see...

35
00:01:33,292 --> 00:01:34,884
Hey, that's a ladder.

36
00:01:34,884 --> 00:01:37,870
That means this is legit,
this might go somewhere.

37
00:01:37,870 --> 00:01:40,612
I mean, it probably leads to a
room filled with poison gas

38
00:01:40,612 --> 00:01:42,949
and a bunch of dead people
who look just like me,

39
00:01:42,949 --> 00:01:46,507
but I don't KNOW that, so
there's room for hope, I guess.

40
00:01:46,507 --> 00:01:50,022
But, yeah, I was expecting to look
down there and see this giant eyeball

41
00:01:50,022 --> 00:01:54,404
looking up at me, angry at me because
I blew off its eyelashes or something,

42
00:01:54,404 --> 00:01:59,217
then the whole building starts shaking
and I guess I'd... just... ball up and cry.

43
00:01:59,217 --> 00:02:02,368
Because, what do you do when
something that big wants to kill you?

44
00:02:02,368 --> 00:02:05,667
I'm used to people being beneath
me, in so many ways.

45
00:02:06,445 --> 00:02:09,932
God, it smells like ass down here!

46
00:02:09,932 --> 00:02:12,980
Maybe I should go back, this is rank!

47
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:16,778
But, then again, I'm not exactly
Crescent Fresh myself.

48
00:02:16,778 --> 00:02:19,897
Well, this experience is enough
to show those chicken people up.

49
00:02:19,897 --> 00:02:23,053
I hate those people who say
every new meat tastes like chicken.

50
00:02:23,053 --> 00:02:25,514
I bet this thing tastes
NOTHING like chicken;

51
00:02:25,514 --> 00:02:27,367
it doesn't smell like cooked chicken.

52
00:02:27,367 --> 00:02:28,434
I bet it tastes like...

53
00:02:29,033 --> 00:02:30,262
...grasshoppers.

54
00:02:30,262 --> 00:02:33,496
I haven't tasted it, but
this thing smells bad.

55
00:02:33,496 --> 00:02:34,923
I'm not going to try it.

56
00:02:34,923 --> 00:02:37,845
Oh... oh, that's a drop.

57
00:02:37,845 --> 00:02:41,885
Wow, this is really making put
my money where my mouth is.

58
00:02:41,885 --> 00:02:44,655
Because earlier I said I wanted
to do a long drop cannonball

59
00:02:44,655 --> 00:02:45,968
if there was water down there.

60
00:02:46,582 --> 00:02:47,395
And here it is.

61
00:02:47,395 --> 00:02:48,495
Uh...

62
00:02:48,495 --> 00:02:50,364
Kind of stupid...

63
00:02:50,364 --> 00:02:53,748
But there's a light down there,
this could be all right...

64
00:02:53,748 --> 00:02:55,333
Let's assess:

65
00:02:55,333 --> 00:02:59,091
Cons: I might starve to death
where nobody could ever find me.

66
00:02:59,091 --> 00:03:01,534
Pros: This could be fun as hell.

67
00:03:02,315 --> 00:03:03,234
I'm going to do it.

68
00:03:04,510 --> 00:03:06,093
Yeeeeeeeeeeeee...!

69
00:03:07,274 --> 00:03:13,067
[underwater mumbling]

70
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:18,234
[gasping, Geiger counter clicking]
Oh... radiation... dead bodies... no...!

71
00:03:20,637 --> 00:03:33,126
[underwater mumbling]

72
00:03:33,126 --> 00:03:36,000
[gasping]

73
00:03:37,069 --> 00:03:41,453
All right! I'm making a lot of progress
for not knowing where the hell I'm going.

74
00:03:41,453 --> 00:03:44,304
And I can breathe.
What more could I want?

75
00:03:44,304 --> 00:03:47,601
Whoa. That's a lot of sludge.

76
00:03:47,601 --> 00:03:48,779
I guess this way.

77
00:03:48,779 --> 00:03:50,017
[Geiger counter clicks]

78
00:03:50,017 --> 00:03:51,601
[Geiger counter clicks]
Wait, this doesn't go anywhere.

79
00:03:52,782 --> 00:03:56,436
JESUS CHRIST! Look at how much
we're pumping out!

80
00:03:56,436 --> 00:03:58,416
This is bad!

81
00:03:58,416 --> 00:04:00,761
I thought the other spills were bad,

82
00:04:00,761 --> 00:04:03,155
but I also thought they
might be kind of contained,

83
00:04:03,155 --> 00:04:06,049
like we had some sort of plan
if this happened,

84
00:04:06,049 --> 00:04:08,095
but this is a river!

85
00:04:08,095 --> 00:04:12,472
I'm not a bleeding-heart ecologist, and
I've got more pressing things on my mind,

86
00:04:12,472 --> 00:04:15,867
but fuck me, if this gets into
the groundwater...

87
00:04:15,867 --> 00:04:20,885
Well, that's it, we've already been playing
crash and burn with this whole facility,

88
00:04:20,885 --> 00:04:25,162
but this is us pissing on the ashes as
our final tribute to the whole community.

89
00:04:25,162 --> 00:04:26,752
I'm getting out of New Mexico.

90
00:04:26,752 --> 00:04:29,246
I don't care what the
agreement on my lease says.

91
00:04:29,246 --> 00:04:31,074
I'm glad I didn't buy a house.

92
00:04:31,074 --> 00:04:34,953
Real estate here is going to be a thing
of the past once cancer rates explode

93
00:04:34,953 --> 00:04:36,809
and two-headed babies start being born.

94
00:04:36,809 --> 00:04:38,736
[Geiger counter clicks]

95
00:04:38,736 --> 00:04:40,274
[Geiger counter clicks]
I'll try going this way.

96
00:04:40,274 --> 00:04:42,445
[Geiger counter clicks]
This is all even worse than it looks.

97
00:04:42,445 --> 00:04:43,558
[Geiger counter clicks]
Because, say we were dumping

98
00:04:43,558 --> 00:04:46,082
[Geiger counter clicks]
barrels of pig shit into the groundwater.

99
00:04:46,082 --> 00:04:47,874
[Geiger counter clicks]
That would not be good,

100
00:04:47,874 --> 00:04:49,407
[Geiger counter clicks]
but at least that's biodegradable

101
00:04:49,407 --> 00:04:51,641
[Geiger counter clicks]
and would eventually decompose over time.

102
00:04:51,641 --> 00:04:52,967
[Geiger counter clicks]
But, no, look at this.

103
00:04:52,967 --> 00:04:54,189
[Geiger counter clicks]
My Geiger counter's ticking and

104
00:04:54,189 --> 00:04:56,074
[Geiger counter clicks]
this stuff is fucking glowing.

105
00:04:56,074 --> 00:04:57,456
[Geiger counter clicks]
That's radioactive.

106
00:04:57,456 --> 00:04:58,840
[Geiger counter clicks]
That's not going anywhere.

107
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:01,381
[Geiger counter clicks]
Radiation is the gift that keeps on giving.

108
00:05:01,381 --> 00:05:02,315
[Geiger counter clicks]

109
00:05:02,315 --> 00:05:04,292
[Geiger counter clicks]
Maybe I should just leave the country,

110
00:05:04,292 --> 00:05:05,737
[Geiger counter clicks]
go back to Austria.

111
00:05:05,737 --> 00:05:06,948
[Geiger counter clicks]
It was nice there.

112
00:05:06,948 --> 00:05:08,518
[Geiger counter clicks]
Plus, I swear half the women there

113
00:05:08,518 --> 00:05:10,093
[Geiger counter clicks]
look like they could be models.

114
00:05:10,093 --> 00:05:11,243
[Geiger counter clicks]
And, of course, there my beard

115
00:05:11,243 --> 00:05:13,282
[Geiger counter clicks]
would get the respect it deserves.

116
00:05:13,282 --> 00:05:14,594
[Geiger counter clicks]
I mean, look at Freud.

117
00:05:14,594 --> 00:05:15,891
[Geiger counter clicks]
He knew what he was doing.

118
00:05:15,891 --> 00:05:19,669
Unlike here where nobody has any style
and everyone looks the same.

119
00:05:19,669 --> 00:05:23,567
Though, I will say that--whoa, long drop.

120
00:05:23,567 --> 00:05:27,193
Wow, this place just
goes down forever, huh?

121
00:05:27,193 --> 00:05:27,901
All right.

122
00:05:29,233 --> 00:05:32,086
Yeah, I will say the Einstein
hair and mustache look

123
00:05:32,086 --> 00:05:35,011
that some people around here are
sporting is pretty happening.

124
00:05:35,011 --> 00:05:38,298
I thought it was a little weird at first
but it's definitely growing on me.

125
00:05:38,298 --> 00:05:39,943
Hey, what's this do?

126
00:05:39,943 --> 00:05:42,260
I bet Einstein got babes.

127
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:44,141
Huh, nothing apparently.

128
00:05:44,141 --> 00:05:47,485
Kind of disappointing, though I guess
that's better it detaching the pipe

129
00:05:47,485 --> 00:05:49,234
and me plummeting to my death.

130
00:05:49,838 --> 00:05:51,987
Oh! Gross! Look at that.

131
00:05:51,987 --> 00:05:55,288
You can see the skin
on top of it like soup!

132
00:05:55,288 --> 00:05:56,716
You know, now that I think about it,

133
00:05:56,716 --> 00:06:01,330
the Einstein look is really just the
Karl Marx look just without the beard.

134
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:03,499
Hey, another pipe entrance!

135
00:06:03,499 --> 00:06:05,973
I am so lost...

136
00:06:05,973 --> 00:06:07,700
Oh, I can clear this gap.

137
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:10,162
I'll just get enough speed
to go around the side.

138
00:06:10,162 --> 00:06:13,968
It'll be just like how I used to pass
people in those tube slides as a kid.

139
00:06:14,746 --> 00:06:16,478
Nnnnyyyyeow!

140
00:06:16,478 --> 00:06:17,502
Awesome.

141
00:06:17,502 --> 00:06:19,911
Yeah, what sucked about doing
that as a kid was that

142
00:06:19,911 --> 00:06:23,715
sometimes there wouldn't be enough clearance
between me and the kid in front of me,

143
00:06:23,715 --> 00:06:28,185
so I'd come at them full-speed and try to
pass, but then we both get wedged in the tube.

144
00:06:28,185 --> 00:06:31,411
Then they would get skin-burns
from rubbing against the plastic,

145
00:06:31,411 --> 00:06:32,836
then they'd start crying,

146
00:06:32,836 --> 00:06:35,916
then the teacher would yell at
me for not waiting my turn,

147
00:06:35,916 --> 00:06:37,891
then I'd get detention...

148
00:06:37,891 --> 00:06:39,334
Hey, what are those green lights?

149
00:06:40,243 --> 00:06:42,987
Huh, I guess it's residue from the waste.

150
00:06:43,783 --> 00:06:44,670
[metal groaning]
But why aren't the--

151
00:06:44,670 --> 00:06:46,167
Oh, shit, shit, SHIT!

152
00:06:47,192 --> 00:06:48,692
Okay. I... aaughh...

153
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:50,126
Ugh...

154
00:06:50,854 --> 00:06:52,025
Well, that works.

155
00:06:54,199 --> 00:06:55,199
Cool.

156
00:06:55,199 --> 00:06:58,436
Our cheap-ass table complements
our cheap-ass pipe,

157
00:06:58,436 --> 00:07:00,634
because now my knees aren't broken.

